25,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems general-purpose spaces are in high demand, while specialist ones sit idle. Also, shared booking spaces are rated much higher by users.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that matches my findings. However, taking rooms out of service is costing us a fortune in off-site rentals. We must be careful.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I've found that ""comfort"" projects often slip by a year, and outdoor work is heavily impacted by weather delays. We should avoid outdoor risks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Mechanical costs are rising fast, and we have no money set aside for replacing old AV kit. The budget is tighter than it looks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks because the equipment is outdated, yet we have no new front-of-house staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, if the equipment is failing the staff, that's a priority. But we can't ignore the student demand for general study space.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if outdoor work is a gamble, that makes me very nervous about any plan involving the campus grounds.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. A project that is ""nice to have"" but slips in schedule is a failure of planning. We need something essential and indoor.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if we do something mechanical, we need to account for that twenty percent price jump I saw in the tenders.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the cost of doing nothing is the manual labor of my staff. We need a functional upgrade, not just a ""nice"" room.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We need to balance the staff's burden with the students' needs. A general-purpose space seems to be the most universally praised model.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"But @Mizuki, the rental costs for displaced students are a huge hidden drain. We need a plan with minimal disruption.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,An indoor conversion of an existing hall might be the safest bet regarding both weather and delivery schedules.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"As long as we don't ignore the equipment costs. If we build a new center, who pays for the gear in five years?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A ventilation upgrade would solve the manual routine issue. It's not ""comfort""; it's a functional necessity for the labs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, is the lab upgrade a ""comfort"" project or a ""finding"" project? Benjamin said the latter are more likely to finish on time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, would a lab upgrade take rooms out of service for a long time? That's my main concern.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"If it's a replacement of essential plant, it's usually treated as a necessity, which helps the schedule.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Kenji,,But the tender records show mechanical plant costs are the ones spiking. That could blow the budget.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It's better to pay the market rate now than to keep paying in staff hours and inefficiency.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
